---
pagination:
  data: gamePages
  size: 1
  alias: game
permalink: "{{ game.url }}"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
lang: en
aiGenerated: true
humanReviewed: false
---
{#- A game page (si-y6pp): one page per game in src/_data/games.json whose
    article this build builds (`gamePages`, scripts/lib/games.mjs), at
    /blog/<article>/<game>-<version>/. It is built like the game page of the
    Gaimer version that made the game: the container's style of that
    version's GameContainer.vue, then the game's code as JSON, then the
    version's page script (sandbox.js and a stand-in for GameContainer.vue,
    game-page-<version>.js in the article's media), which loads the game into
    a sandboxed frame the size of the window. The page is the game and
    nothing else, and it is in English like the games, so it has no header,
    navigation or footer, no skip link, no language switch and no
    counterpart; the gates hold it to the rules that fit it (gamePagePaths
    in scripts/lib/games.mjs). Like every page it links the English feed in
    its head, and it names the site's default image for a link preview
    (si-awlu), as every page that is not an article does. The h1 names the
    game for a screen reader and is not shown. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ game.title }} — {{ strings.en.site.name }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ game.description }}">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ game.title }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ game.description }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:locale" content="en_GB">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ strings.en.site.name }}">
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ shareImage.url | absoluteUrl(site.url) }}">
  <meta property="og:image:type" content="{{ shareImage.type }}">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ shareImage.width }}">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ shareImage.height }}">
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ strings.en.site.imageAlt }}">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="{{ strings.en.site.imageAlt }}">
  <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="{{ strings.en.feed.title }}" href="{{ feedUrl | absoluteUrl(site.url) }}">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
  <style>
    html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; background: #1a1a1a; }
    .game-title { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); }
{%- if game.version == "before" %}
    .game-canvas-wrapper { width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #1a1a1a; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; }
    .game-canvas-wrapper iframe { max-width: 100%; max-height: 100%; }
{%- else %}
    .game-canvas-wrapper { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #1a1a1a; }
{%- endif %}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main id="game" class="game-canvas-wrapper">
    <h1 class="game-title">{{ game.title }}</h1>
  </main>
  <script type="application/json" id="game-code">{{ game.code | jsonScript | safe }}</script>
  <script src="{{ game.script }}"></script>
</body>
</html>
